<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mbanza Kongo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mbanza <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kongo</a> is a town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a>, the capital of the Kingdom of Kongo. According to tradition it was founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lukeni-lua-nimi">Lukeni lua Nimi</a>. It was renamed Sao <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a> after the kingdom's conversion to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and is now a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mbanza-kongo.jpg" alt="Mbanza Kongo" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Astley · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Bansa,_or_residence_of_the_King_of_Kongo,_called_St._Salvador_(M%27Banza_Kongo),_Astley_1745.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
